1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,854
Rita: Thirty more seconds?

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,287
Ned: Phil? I’ve got a policy that—

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:10,611
DJ: Rise and shine, campers! Tuesday, February second!

4
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:12,461
Phil: That’s... the Groundhog Day situation.

5
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,830
Phil: I’m stuck in a loop.

6
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:18,787
Phil: Test the theory. Not the coach. Not the couch. The piano.

7
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:24,157
Phil: I sit down and I play, badly, and I stay until my fingers remember a shape I do not own.

8
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:32,229
Phil: The couch is a couch. It does not move itself.

9
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:37,776
Phil: It’s Phil. I’m in Pittsburgh. The van is confirmed for eight A.M. I’ll be there.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,054
DJ: Tuesday, February second.

11
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,545
Phil: I was there. She heard me.

12
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:45,558
Phil: Rita, Larry—see you at the party. I’m heading to Pittsburgh.

13
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,484
Rita: Morning, Phil.

14
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:54,730
Phil: About last—

15
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:56,416
Phil: Snow till noon.

16
00:00:59,270 --> 00:01:04,830
Phil: The curtains are closed. I’ve spent the afternoon in bed. Again.

17
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:09,749
Phil: The loop has done this to me so many times I can barely feel the texture of the sheets anymore.

18
00:01:16,130 --> 00:01:17,537
Ned: It covers the whole year.

19
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,148
Phil: I’ll take it.

20
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,800
Rita: You sold one?

21
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,210
Ned: To Phil. I forgot my pen.

22
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,810
Ned: He waited.

23
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:35,803
Rita: I’m putting it on the wire.

24
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,940
Phil: There are two more bars.

25
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:42,761
Rita: Save those for the morning.

26
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,880
Rita: You owe me two bars.

27
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:47,664
DJ: Wednesday.

